{"id": "tea:amrtasiddhi:topic.avasthas", "source": "src:amrtasiddhi", "location": {"ref": "topic.avasthas"}, "paraphrase": "Four stages of the practice are taught — ārambha, ghaṭa, paricaya and niṣpatti — each with its signs, culminating in the yogin's perfection.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "powers-experiences"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D).", "concepts": ["cpt:four-avasthas-of-yoga"], "paths": ["pth:hatha-four-stages"], "terms": ["trm:arambha", "trm:ghata", "trm:paricaya", "trm:nispatti"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtasiddhi:topic.bindu", "source": "src:amrtasiddhi", "location": {"ref": "topic.bindu"}, "paraphrase": "Bindu is the essence of the body and the source of life; it is the moon; as long as bindu is stable the body lives, and its falling is death.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers", "death-dying"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D).", "concepts": ["cpt:bindu", "cpt:bindu-natha"], "terms": ["trm:bindu", "trm:candra"], "obstacles": ["obs:bindu-pata"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtasiddhi:topic.madhyama", "source": "src:amrtasiddhi", "location": {"ref": "topic.madhyama"}, "paraphrase": "The central channel (madhyamā) is where sun and moon are to be united; when the breath enters it the yogin attains the state of immortality.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D). The Amṛtasiddhi's own names for the channels (madhyamā etc.) recalled with low confidence.", "concepts": ["cpt:susumna-central-channel"], "terms": ["trm:susumna"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtasiddhi:topic.sun-moon", "source": "src:amrtasiddhi", "location": {"ref": "topic.sun-moon"}, "paraphrase": "The moon in the head continually drips nectar, which the sun (fire) in the belly consumes; this consumption is the cause of ageing and death; the yogin's task is to prevent it.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "causal", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["body-layers", "death-dying"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D).", "concepts": ["cpt:sun-moon-fire", "cpt:amrta-natha"], "terms": ["trm:surya", "trm:candra", "trm:amrta"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:amrtasiddhi:topic.three-mudras", "source": "src:amrtasiddhi", "location": {"ref": "topic.three-mudras"}, "paraphrase": "The text teaches three practices — mahāmudrā, mahābandha and mahāvedha — by which the breath is forced into the central channel and bindu is made steady; it is the first known text to teach them.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U28-hatha-texts"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "coverage": ["A10", "D"], "notes": "Topic-level locator: exact chapter/verse not recalled (to be supplied in Phase D). The 'first known' claim is the scholarly account (Mallinson & Szántó), not the text's.", "practices": ["prc:mahamudra", "prc:mahabandha", "prc:mahavedha"], "concepts": ["cpt:bindu-natha"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U28-hatha-texts"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
